# Client configuration.
#
# Every network key below is required: `getConfig()` refuses rather than
# defaulting to a network nobody chose. The two brand keys at the end are
# optional, and unset means the index. Note these are compiled INTO the bundle
# at build time, not read at runtime -- a build made for TestNet cannot be
# repointed at MainNet by changing a variable on the host. It has to be rebuilt.

# CAIP-2 network identifier: the literal string x402 uses, which is
# "algorand:" plus the base64 genesis hash -- NOT the transaction's
# genesisID ("testnet-v1.0"). The two are easy to confuse and only one of
# them will match a 402's `network` field.
VITE_NETWORK=algorand:SGO1GKSzyE7IEPItTxCByw9x8FmnrCDexi9/cOUJOiI=

# Payment asset. TestNet USDC is 10458941; MainNet USDC is 31566704.
VITE_ASSET_ID=10458941

# The escrow application id. Cannot be recovered from the 402 -- that carries
# payTo, the application *account*, and deriving an id from an account is
# one-way. The client asserts the two agree before building any group.
VITE_APP_ID=

# The x402 facilitator.
VITE_FACILITATOR_URL=

# Origin the paid route is served from. https, except on localhost.
VITE_RESOURCE_HOST=

# Must equal the server's MAX_FILE_BYTES. The client refuses an oversized file
# before the unpaid pass, because that pass commits an agreement on chain and
# parks its deposit -- quoting a file that cannot complete loses that deposit
# for nothing. Mirrored here and known to drift; the durable home is the paid
# route's discovery input schema, which a buyer agent already reads.
VITE_MAX_FILE_BYTES=16777216

# The chain, read directly. Everything a buyer needs after paying -- did the
# pool fill, was the edition delivered, can I have my money back -- is state on
# chain, and the paid route answers none of it.
#
# TestNet: https://testnet-api.4160.nodely.dev  /  https://testnet-idx.4160.nodely.dev
# MainNet: https://mainnet-api.4160.nodely.dev  /  https://mainnet-idx.4160.nodely.dev
#
# These must name the same network as VITE_NETWORK. The client checks: the
# suggested params it already fetches carry a genesis hash, and a mismatch
# refuses before anything is signed.
VITE_ALGOD_URL=

# Used for three questions, all answered from the application's history: which
# pools a buyer joined, when they arrive without their link; how a closed pool
# ended, since closing deletes the boxes that would say; and where a released
# pool's edition is, since the note on its release is the link's only record.
# Every pool read is algod, so an unreachable indexer costs those three answers
# -- recovery degrades to "open your link", a closed pool reads as gone, and a
# released pool says its link cannot be read right now -- and nothing else.
VITE_INDEXER_URL=

# The IPFS gateway a released pool's edition link is resolved against: an
# https origin, with no path, no credentials and no trailing slash (this page
# adds /ipfs/<cid>/edition-<N>.html itself). Never on chain -- the release note
# records a CID, and which gateway turns it into a link is this build's choice.
#
# e.g. https://ipfs.filebase.io
#
# Pick one that serves plain HTTP fetches. ipfs.io, dweb.link and w3s.link
# stop doing so on 2026-09-21, and throttle them in the weeks before; a build
# pointed at one of them shows buyers a link that does not open.
VITE_IPFS_GATEWAY=

# Optional. Which product line the page presents: `index` (the default, when
# unset or empty) or `travel`. Read on its own by `getBrand()`, never through
# `getConfig()`, and anything else refuses to start. `travel` runs on TestNet
# only: with any other VITE_NETWORK, LocalNet included, it refuses to start.
VITE_BRAND=

# Optional, travel only: the sample trip the page shows, as the base64 of UTF-8
# JSON (shape and limits in `src/config.ts`, `parseOffer`). Display text only:
# the seat price, the seat count and the deadline are the agreement's, never
# the offer's. Its optional `provider` field is the data source's display
# name, shown in the fare's caption and the demo notice; without it the page
# names no data source. An offer that is off-shape, or one given to the index,
# refuses to start with the configuration error naming the field. Supplied at
# build time and never committed.
VITE_OFFER_B64=
